# Maze's End on its second turn: "{3}, {T}, Return this land to its owner's hand" is paid as the ability is activated, so the
# land is already in Bot1's hand when it resolves; then "Search your library for a Gate card, put it onto the battlefield, then
# shuffle": a Gate may be taken (Azorius Guildgate, which enters tapped - it is one more land, not an untapped one), a
# non-Gate card (Island) is refused. With one Gate only, the ten-different-Gates condition is false and the game goes on.

[Bot1 Deck]
Maze's End
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Island x3
Island x8
Azorius Guildgate
Island x8

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Maze's End.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Maze's End.Activate(Ability: Return)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Hand = Island; Island; Island; Island; Maze's End
! Bot1.Search(Island)
Bot1.Search(Azorius Guildgate)

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Azorius Guildgate.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Azorius Guildgate.Subtypes = Gate
Result = InProgress
